what is the style sheet or  guide to write python?
PEP8

\n -  new line
\t - gives one tab space
\b -  remove one letter backward ('hello\bworld') , o/p :hellworld
\f -  new line
\r - executes right side ('hello\rworld') , o/p : world
\v - makes the first letter of word in UPPERCASE , ('hello\vworld') , o/p : helloWorld ('w'in caps)

when "use \ with characters like ( \n,\v,\b,\f,\r,\v) " python  will consider this as Special characters.

